<div class="s-faq" data-plr-component="s-faq">
  <div class="u-container">
    <div class="s__header">
      <h2 class="s__title t-h-sm">FAQs</h2>
      <div class="s__line"></div>
      <p class="s__intro">
        Find answers to common questions about our coding bootcamp, courses,
        admissions, and more.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="s__questions">
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          What kind of support can I expect as a student at Nod?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            We are here to support you all the way, we know how to turn
            beginners into proficient programmers as quickly as possible. We’ll
            support you when you struggle and push you when you’re comfortable
            ;)
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          How skilled will I be upon graduating from Nod?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            You can expect to be skilled enough to pass a technical interview
            and land a job in tech. More importantly, you will have the skills
            to quickly learn and apply new programming concepts on your own.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          How does the admissions process work?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            1. Apply with the form on this site. 2. We contact you to schedule a
            short digital meeting . 3. At the meeting, we’ll assess if you’ve
            got the right motivation for the bootcamp. You’ll also get to ask
            any questions about the bootcamp. 4. Technical interview takes place
            (you will get access to study material to be prepped, don’t worry).
            5. Sign our Student Agreement and pay the registration fee to
            officially secure your seat.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          How much programming experience do I need to be accepted to the
          bootcamp?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            No prior programming experience is required. However, many of our
            students have taken a programming course in university or dabble
            with Python on Codecademy or Udemy. Having previous experience
            definitely helps, but it’s not mandatory. Completing the prep work
            ensures everyone is on a similar level when we start.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          What is the maximum number of students per cohort?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            No more than 12 students to give you the best possible learning
            experience. If small classes, you are more likely to engage with the
            material, ask questions, and express your thoughts. You will also
            feel more accountable for your participation and performance, making
            you put in that extra effort to do your best. As for us instructors,
            we can interact more personally with you and provide tailored
            feedback.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          Does Nod guarantee that I’ll find a job?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            No, but we have an 87% hiring rate. Pivoting careers is tough and
            requires a lot of effort on your part. We will provide you with the
            technical skills to ace the interview and extensive career support
            to make you stand out online.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          What jobs do your alumni land after the bootcamp?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            Data Analyst, Data Science and Data Engineer positions are the most
            common.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          What financing options are there?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            Typically, you’d pay the tuition fee via bank transfer (or Swish if
            you’re Swedish). We also accept Bitcoin and PayPal, but you pay for
            the transaction fee using these options. The tuition is paid 10 days
            before the bootcamp starts and in some cases, we have agreed on a
            split payment.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sb-question js-question">
        <h3 class="sb__question">
          <span
            class="a-bullet-point a-bullet-point--outline a-bullet-point--blue"
          ></span>

          Will I get a certificate when graduating from Nod?
        </h3>
        <div class="sb__inner js-inner">
          <div class="sb__answer t-t-sm rte js-answer">
            Upon completion, you’ll get an impressive blockchain certificate.
            But we are more about ensuring you acquire the hands-on skills to
            pass technical interviews and excel in a Data Analyst or Data
            Scientist role.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sb__icon">
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
          <div class="sb__icon__line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
